{:edb/db-before-t 2199 :edb/db-after-t 2200 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535512 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:33:11.903Z" 13194139535512 true] [17592186129198 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352994 13194139535512 true] [17592186129217 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353015 13194139535512 true] [17592186129218 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353001 13194139535512 true] [17592186129218 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353008 13194139535512 true] [17592186129442 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535512 true] [17592186129442 1100 "For the transformation $T$, defined as\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2u\\cos v \\\\ 3u\\sin v\\end{bmatrix}$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535512 false] [17592186129442 1100 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535512 true] [17592186129442 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$ and $y(u,v)=3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot 3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-(-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =6u({cos}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v) \\\\  & =6u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,2)}=6(1)=6.\n$$" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352994 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352995 13194139535512 true] [17592186352994 1089 "q-160427" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352994 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535512 true] [17592186352994 1100 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ {u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352994 1113 #uuid "358311d9-2c61-59cc-ac39-8891f3d6b2ae" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352994 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2v \\\\ 2u & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2v)-2v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-4uv-4uv \\\\  & =-8uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-2,1)}=-8(-2)(1)=16.\n$$" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352996 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352997 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352998 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352999 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353000 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1041 "selection" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352998 13194139535512 true] [17592186352995 1110 #uuid "6a70ac85-cca7-5847-8ac7-2f1243b716d6" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352996 1034 "12" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186352996 1111 #uuid "c78e50f2-df92-5d32-b021-3678fecb2653" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352997 1034 "-8" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186352997 1111 #uuid "82b14d9a-5b24-5452-bb9e-25b311f1c6df" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352998 1034 "16" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186352998 1111 #uuid "57f39cb0-b84e-55cd-83ee-42d45899064c" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352999 1034 "14" 13194139535512 true] [17592186352999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186352999 1111 #uuid "a6588f46-d395-578b-acd2-0c57d12e187e" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353000 1034 "18" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186353000 1111 #uuid "674dad15-21e8-5183-a4b7-782ee5898f24" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353001 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353002 13194139535512 true] [17592186353001 1089 "q-161843" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353001 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535512 true] [17592186353001 1100 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353001 1113 #uuid "4a1b487f-874e-5662-8cb4-0ff2c90e3298" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353001 1145 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2v \\\\ -2u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1-(-2u)\\cdot (2v) \\\\  & =4+4uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+4uv & >0 \\\\ 4uv & >-4 \\\\ uv & >-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the solution $v>-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u>0$ and $v<-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u<0.$\n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-\\frac{1}{u}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,1)$ and $(-1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariab