the solution $v>\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u>0$ and $v<\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u<0.$\n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{u}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,2)$ and $(-1,-2)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n   \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png)" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353010 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353011 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353012 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353013 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353014 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1041 "selection" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353012 13194139535512 true] [17592186353009 1110 #uuid "1241b385-e434-5aec-b1e8-a0c74101ae4a" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353010 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/4d944eb13437b86c0cf6ae4fa8bca09031ed0f2f85a9f20bcb0050a6de9f8ebb.png" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353010 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535512 true] [17592186353010 1111 #uuid "1b38b5a8-fcd3-5729-95f3-d2b67868d894" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353011 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535512 true] [17592186353011 1111 #uuid "e2710562-98ac-5e9b-bb7e-966ec4f09f49" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353012 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535512 true] [17592186353012 1111 #uuid "fd1def52-dd46-56d3-9c0f-d25733d66390" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353013 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535512 true] [17592186353013 1111 #uuid "3c7311c2-b4c7-5f25-887d-9d8a7656ca4d" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353014 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/f7bc22ac4dfd2d7015952144ece63f91ecccef2a992649aece60dc8a70f1d018.png" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535512 true] [17592186353014 1111 #uuid "4b30bfe3-68ef-50a0-86ca-f51df375ec2b" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353015 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353016 13194139535512 true] [17592186353015 1089 "q-161873" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353015 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535512 true] [17592186353015 1100 "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u}-v \\\\ {u}^{2}v\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353015 1113 #uuid "9c4b0cb3-e283-5cdd-b9d4-c83ef946d645" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353015 1145 "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}} & -1 \\\\ 2uv & {u}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}})\\cdot ({u}^{2})-2uv\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-1+2uv \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(2,2)} & =(-1+2uv)\\,{|}_{u=2\\,v=2} \\\\  & =-1+2(2)(2) \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|7|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =7\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353017 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353018 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353019 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353020 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353021 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1041 "selection" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353021 13194139535512 true] [17592186353016 1110 #uuid "b92581a9-0527-5110-b05f-748971ebd883" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353017 1034 "5\\,\\delta A" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186353017 1111 #uuid "4cc7022d-903a-524c-a8ea-addf0b82c712" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353018 1034 "6\\,\\delta A" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186353018 1111 #uuid "e5908624-e088-5502-9da6-fc83b968a98b" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353019 1034 "14\\,\\delta A" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535512 true] [17592186353019 1111 #uuid "c684e0eb-7993-5acb-9c53-331e6b7f10a2" 13194139535512 true] [17592186353020 1034 "9\\,\\delta A"